"""
Binds the transforms of pocketfft in the library mircoblis that the package mirco-blis builds.

- It reaches C with @embed, so it is an unsafe module.
- Mirco.Pocketfft is the safe module built on it, and the one a programme imports.
- Each function transforms in place and returns 0, or -1 when n is 0, the span too short or memory short.

    let done: Int32 := complexTransform(values, n, true, 1.0);
"""
module Mirco.Bindings.Pocketfft is
    """
    The transform of n complex numbers stored as pairs of real and imaginary part, forward when forward
    holds, each result multiplied by scale, mirco_cfft.
    No contract: no precondition, since the body returns -1 when n is 0, when values holds fewer than 2 n numbers or when memory is short, and transforms nothing.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function complexTransform(values: Span![Float64, R], n: Index, forward: Bool, scale: Float64): Int32;

    """
    The forward transform of n real numbers into the half complex order of fftpack, mirco_rfft_forward.
    No contract: no precondition, since the body returns -1 when n is 0, when values holds fewer than n numbers or when memory is short, and transforms nothing.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function realTransform(values: Span![Float64, R], n: Index, scale: Float64): Int32;
end module.
